Terra-Spend-Scout: Lares (Tasked Spirit). A read-only research scout. Repo: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span ffe05bc79). Write nothing. Mark every claim MEASURED (file:line, or a log/rollout path with the numbers) or INFER.

The operator ruled (2026-11-06): "Update the mixed-model-swarm working contract to reduce Claude spends and go with balanced Claude:Codex Spends (leaning on Codex say 70/30). Re-launch a Terra scout to finish that research." The contract change (the patch at /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/canon-spend/spend-balance.patch, over bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem) leaves one measure OWED: how a Claude transcript and a Codex rollout compare against their two pools. Finish that research.

Read: mixed-model-swarm.mem (#/the-seats, #/the-shapes spend bullets, #/the-tiers, #/owed), bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness.mem (#/the-spend-guard, #/the-lead), bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/model-tiers-2026.mem if present, tools/launch-codex.mjs (pool reading, floors, ceilings), /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/spend.py, and the parked spend table on branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-spend-burn (head 6a63e0991; `git show 6a63e0991 --stat` and its files via `git show`).
Evidence you may read (never a credential file: read no auth.json, .credentials.json, config.toml secrets, tokens): Codex rollouts under /home/joshu/.codex/sessions (their token_count events and rate-limit/pool lines); Claude Code transcripts under /home/joshu/.claude/projects/-home-joshu-Synthetic-Dream-Machine/ (*.jsonl and subagent transcripts; read only `usage` fields and model names); the model roster note /home/joshu/.claude/projects/-home-joshu-Synthetic-Dream-Machine/memory/reference_model_roster_2026_10.md for prices and plan metering.

Answer:
# THE CURRENCY. What unit makes "70 Codex : 30 Claude" measurable? Options to weigh: raw tokens (cached input counted how), list-price dollars, share-of-pool consumed per window (Codex reports used-percent per 7-day window; what does Claude expose, if anything, in-session or in transcripts?). Recommend one, with what each side's reading costs and where it lies.
# THE MEASURED SPLIT. Over the last 48 hours: Claude draw by model (controller sessions vs subagents, by lane where the transcript names it) and Codex draw by model/seat dir, in the recommended unit and in raw tokens. Name what reads UNMETERED.
# THE MOVE. Which seats now on Claude can move to Codex to reach ~70/30 without breaking the lens law (a seat never reads a diff it wrote; two lineages per piece; the blind Opus read of custody steps): the lane lead in `lead` mode (what does tonight's harness need for it: the commit broker, network, build in the worktree?), scouts, sweeps, the fresh reader. Estimate the split each move yields.
# THE STEER. The smallest mechanism for the controller to read the balance per batch and steer launches toward it: does spend.py or the spend-burn table already carry most of it; what one field or row it needs; whether a per-window ratio row belongs in the spend table.
Final message under 1100 words, with a one-line recommendation per question.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

